  "plain_text": "USB Creation Tools\nMiniOS can be installed to a USB drive using various tools depending on your operating system.\nRecommended Tools\nWindows\nRufus - Reliable and versatile. Recommended for most users.\nBalena Etcher - Simple, cross-platform, modern interface.\nVentoy - Allows placing multiple ISOs on one drive without reformatting.\nLinux\ndd command - Universal command-line tool. Fast and pre-installed on most distros.\nBalena Etcher - Easy graphical interface.\nFile-based USB installation - Copy MiniOS files manually and install the SYSLINUX bootloader.\nmacOS\nBalena Etcher - The easiest way for Mac users.\ndd command - For advanced users comfortable with the terminal.\nOther Tools\nUNetbootin - A classic tool, though sometimes less reliable with modern ISOs.\nDrive Utility - GNOME Disks or similar built-in utilities.",
  "product_kind": "minios-markup-document",
  "schema_version": 1
}
